{
  "id": 76439657,
  "iid": 814,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "STUN: fix heuristic over TCP",
  "description": "STUN heuristic over TCP (added in 770872790d) doesn't handle multiple STUN messages in the same TCP payload.\n\nWhile at it, added a comment (forgotten in 354bbbe7) about different TURN channel support among STUN versions\n\nYou can reproduce the issue with [stun_tcp_multiple_messages.pcapng](/uploads/427d57b2b307a9d188e3d38dac648eb9/stun_tcp_multiple_messages.pcapng)\n\nThis patch fixes the issue, but it introduces an asymmetry in the heuristic logic:\n* UDP heuristic: we switch to no-heuristic dissector after the first TURN message\n* TCP heuristic: we switch to no-heuristic dissector after the first message different than TURN ChannelData\n\nIs that fine?",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2020-11-01T15:07:56.397Z",
  "updated_at": "2025-06-02T01:02:04.121Z",
